WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.500
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.400
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:24.040
You are my sun now

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.460
We all go through bad times

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.460
no matter who you are

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.890
So don't go hanging your head and feeling down

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:45.560
Keep your head up until your heart's sky

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.980
is clear again

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.320
No matter where you are in this world

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.830
if you're crying and trembling all alone

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:05.160
I'll search for you, I promise

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.830
Love will show me the way

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:16.680
The sun dreams countless times

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:23.520
Forever and always from the horizon

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:30.860
Its shining light gives energy

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:38.240
After all, you are my sun now

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.290
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:03.200
<i>Together with my companions, Barda and Jasmine, I defeated
several terrifying monsters and recovered six gems.</i>

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.760
<i>But to be honest, when I left the Forests of Silence to go on a journey with a stubborn old guy,</i>

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:07.730
<i>Hey!</i>

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.300
<i>along with this unreliable boy,</i>

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.300
<i>What was that?</i>

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.600
<i>I could only hope that
everything would be alright.</i>

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.170
<i>But by working together,
we've finally made it this far!</i>

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.200
<i>There's only one gem remaining!</i>

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.770
<i>Our last perilous destination, The Valley of the Lost
where the diamond is hidden, is just right ahead!</i>

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.200
Hey, why don't we rest for a bit?

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.800
No, let's push forward just a bit further.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.200
It's best to cover as much ground
as possible while it's still daylight.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:49.510
Yeah. The Shadow Army must
still be nearby, searching for us.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.300
I suppose so...

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:53.550
What is it?

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.900
Somebody's coming.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.400
That's what the trees are whispering.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.800
Grey Guards?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.700
A girl?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.800
Alone?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.200
A girl?

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.800
Ouch!

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.900
Oh, come on!

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.000
Neridah?!

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.800
Thank goodness! We're finally reunited!

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.700
W-Wait, Neridah?!

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.000
What's going on?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.600
Weren't you supposed to be with Doom?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.600
I broke up with Doom.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.650
Broke up?!

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.920
Yes. I'm sick of fighting.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.400
So I decided to quit the
Resistance and return home.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.400
You know, Lief... travelling
by myself is so lonely.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.100
Please take me with you!

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.900
Alright, alright that's enough!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.500
Can I help you with something?

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:47.900
Listen, we have somewhere that
we need to go, no matter what.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.500
The Valley of the Lost, right? I know.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.800
I don't mind coming for only part
of the way. Well? Please, Lief?

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.100
Eh? S-Sure... I don't see why not,
if it's only for part of the way...

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.960
Hooray! I knew you would
let me, Lief! I love you!

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.900
Hold on, Lief!

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:10.700
Well, if it was okay for Dain to join us, then
it would be strange to exclude Neridah.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.400
Wow, what a beautiful flower! Look!

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.400
I wonder what kind of flower this is.
Hey Lief, do you know?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.400
Don't call out so loudly.
If the enemy hears you...

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.150
Sorry...

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.200
N-no, it's not really your fault or anything.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.600
Honestly.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:38.200
What was that nonsense about 'a girl travelling alone
would be lonely'? You made it to the finals in Rithmere!

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:45.100
I grew up in a poor village, and was forced
into learning martial arts to make money.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.800
I don't actually like fighting.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.630
Well, nobody actually <i>likes</i> fighting.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.400
By the way, I'm tired.
How about we take a rest?

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.180
Y-Yeah, sure. Let's rest for a bit.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.500
Alright, hooray!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.500
Weren't we supposed to keep
going while we still have daylight?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.600
I'm so hungry!

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.100
Is it ready yet?

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.900
Here, Lief. Have a bite!

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:22.000
N-No, I'm fine. If you don't eat properly, you won't
have the strength to continue on our journey.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.000
But I hate this stuff.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.300
For someone who grew up poor,
you sure act like a spoilt rich girl.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.450
What was that?

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.500
Nothing.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:35.500
Now, now, let's all get
along with one another.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:40.700
Anyway, here Lief. Say 'aa'.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:41.900
Just be patient for now. We will
part ways with her tomorrow.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.900
N-No, like I said, uh...

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.400
Just hold out until then, alright?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.600
Does it taste good?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:45.800
Yeah...

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.500
There's still lots more!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.800
There should be a road leading to
your village just past this slope.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.600
This is where we part ways.
Be careful, Neridah.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:01.500
Right...

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.500
A-Actually no, I will go with Lief for a bit longer!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:06.850
Now, let's go!

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.800
Hey, wait!

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.900
Hurry up!

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.150
Wait! Wait, Neridah!

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.960
What the hell?!

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.100
Hey guys, what are you doing?

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.200
Hurry up and get in here.
The water feels good!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.400
Y-Yeah. Just wait for a bit longer, okay?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.200
You said it was just for one night, didn't you?

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.900
You've got to be kidding! That girl must be
planning to go with us to the Valley of the Lost!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:35.150
Calm down. Keep your head cool.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:37.600
No, you should be the ones
cooling your damn heads!

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.300
I can't trust her! She's even worse than Doom!

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.100
We're not taking her any further than this!

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:47.800
We understand that, but...

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.120
What?

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.300
Oh, uh, nothing.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:55.400
Now that it's come to this, there are only two possible solutions. Pick one.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.400
Number 1: Punch her and run.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.900
Number 2: Throw her into the river and run.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.300
Now, which one?

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.900
W-Well, those choices are a bit...

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.800
I can't punch a girl!

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.650
Then, Number 3: Tie her to a tree and run.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.300
I recommend Number 3.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:19.000
Alright. I will take responsibility for
this and figure something out.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:24.900
Therefore, we can't take
you with us any further.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.540
No way! Why? How cruel!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.040
Lief!

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:34.400
Neridah, please understand. We have
something that we must do no matter what.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:39.200
If that's the case, then I will help you!
I want to lend you my strength, Lief!

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.100
Well? Please?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.800
If there's anything I can do, then...

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.000
Well, about that...

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.100
Geez!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.300
A gold coin!

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.800
Wait!!

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:56.900
Now!

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.600
Where are you, little gold coin?

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.800
My little gold coin?!

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.000
I found it!

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:10.900
Hang on, where's everyone? Lief!

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.300
Where did you go?

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.800
Let's go while she's distracted. Quickly!

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.700
They got me.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.600
I've been completely had.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.900
Honestly, what's wrong with that woman?
She's always getting in the way.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:38.400
I'm sure she's going after the diamond too.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.510
What are you doing out here, Young Lady?

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:57.000
Actually, I became separated
from my friends in the forest,

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.540
and I don't know what to do.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.100
Oh my, that's terrible.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.300
Please! Take me to the Valley of the Lost!

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.140
Why, it would be my pleasure.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.500
Now, let's go.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:12.390
Thank you!

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.400
This is the Valley of the Lost?

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.800
I can't see a thing through this fog.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.400
What's wrong, Kree?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:31.800
These two seem to really dislike this valley.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.800
So, what should we do?

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.540
You two wait here.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.600
If anything happens, please help each other.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.510
Jasmine...

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.720
I can't take Kree and Filli into that place.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:54.000
Don't worry. I promise that we'll return.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.270
Okay, let's go!

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.600
This must be the valley floor.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.100
It's so foggy...

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.700
I can't see anything.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.000
Who are these people?!

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.100
This is bad. There's so many of them.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:20.100
But,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.000
they don't seem to be attacking us.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:30.100
Please, be at ease. Those who reside
in my valley will not harm you.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:34.000
They want nothing more than to
feel the warmth of your souls.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.600
Welcome to the Valley of the Lost.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.200
It has been quite some time...

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.400
...since I last had guests.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.700
Who are you?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.600
I am the Guardian, the custodian
of the Valley of the Lost.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.200
You are searching for the
diamond, are you not?

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.200
Allow me to invite you to my residence.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:02.400
There, we will play a game where your victory will see you rewarded with the diamond. Follow me.

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:03.800
A game?

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:06.000
Either way, let's just follow him for now.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:20.930
What say you? Is this not
a palace worthy of a king?

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:45.200
Oh dear, I apologise. These are my pets.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:53.900
You need not understand it, but they are Pride,
Lie, Envy, and Greed; quite adorable names.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.260
Adorable?!

00:11:55.950 --> 00:12:05.020
Each of them possess a strong trait
of pride, deceit, envy, and greed.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.610
However, their names do not match those traits.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:18.100
For instance, Envy has never been envious of anything
in his life, nor does he possess a strong sense of pride.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.600
Intriguing, is it not?

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.170
Come now! Can you two not behave yourselves?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:42.000
Greed is feared by both the skilled liar, as well as the one with immense pride,

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:45.900
but having said that, they can't
help but fight from time to time.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:52.300
Oh yes, and the greedy one was very
nearly killed by Pride once in the past.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:04.100
I was born to a wealthy household.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:11.100
But, my servants betrayed me. I lost my house, my riches, and everything else.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:16.000
I fled to this valley of solitude and despair.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:22.900
And thus, I was reborn anew as the Guardian of this
valley, through the power of an immense individual.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.520
The Shadow Lord?

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:30.560
I found my answers here. The light will betray me.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.900
But darkness imparts power unto me.

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:42.100
This is a place where sinful
souls wander for eternity.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:45.900
Those who were driven from their homelands on account of their conceitedness,

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:52.600
and the greedy who have eyes for the diamond
which I possess, and seek to take it for themselves!

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.500
Now then, let the game begin!

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:13.900
The diamond you are searching for is in that room.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:20.700
Should you manage to win this game,
you may have the diamond.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:25.800
The door is sealed with magic.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:29.500
It cannot be opened until the game is won.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:35.800
If we win, we will take the diamond,
and leave this valley unharmed.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.600
You agree to that, right?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:39.800
I do not tell lies.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.400
What if we lose?

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.000
If you lose, you will become my subjects.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:53.660
You will become one with the valley for your
greed, and become lost in the fog forever.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.800
So we will become like those things?

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:02.000
Will you accept my challenge?

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.750
Yes, we accept.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.530
Lief!

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.500
It's okay.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:09.900
We've been through so much to get this far.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:14.000
If the three of us work together,
we will be able to overcome this also.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.100
Well said. Now then, allow
me to explain the rules.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:23.800
Why, it's nothing but a word game.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:29.000
Before this candle burns out, guess my name.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.900
If you can do this, that door will open.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:35.300
We really just have to guess your name?

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:39.600
Indeed. Think carefully on the matter.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.300
The first clue exists within this room.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:51.100
It is hidden in a way, but also easy to
find, much like the nose on your face.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:55.500
Now, I will be resting in the next room.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.000
This is the Valley of the Lost.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.500
It looks like a really scary place.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:06.500
From this point on, you will be on your own.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.200
Huh? No way! Why?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:12.300
Unfortunately, I cannot go with you.

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:17.000
But, rest assured. If anything
happens, I will come.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.300
Orcus? Orcus?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.800
Where are you?!

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:27.400
Don't leave me alone!

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:28.700
Tch!

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.300
Why is everyone running from me?

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:36.800
Well, as long as I get the diamond,
I won't need him anyway.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.700
It's no use. There's nothing
written about his name in these.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.050
We should just force our way in, then.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.800
We can't do that, Barda.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.550
But...

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:54.300
The diamond hates violence and dishonesty.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.000
There's even a 'Belt of Deltora' here!

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.200
But, this isn't the book we need right now.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:05.000
It's not like we're trying to steal
the gem out of greed here!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:09.400
But the Guardian said that the door
won't open through brute force.

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:14.000
It may be better to just put our heads
together and find the answer.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:21.500
"It is hidden in a way, but also easy to
find, much like the nose on your face."

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.800
The nose on your face, huh?

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:27.340
It's certainly obvious but it's not something
that one can see for themselves.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:30.200
I get it! The mirror!

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:35.200
One can just use a mirror
to see their own nose!

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:36.850
I see!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.850
There's something here...

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.610
There's writing!

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:46.300
"My secret name awaits within.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:49.200
My first, the name of the immensely prideful.

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.250
My second and fourth begin
with the error in the twin.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:55.100
My third begins a sparkle bright.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:58.000
The end is the beginning, the last has two.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.600
Five letters in total. Guess it correctly."

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.000
So it's a puzzle.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.900
Well to start with, we know that the
Guardian's name is five letters long, right?

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:10.200
The first letter is the name
of the one with immense pride.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.720
Could it be the Guardian's pet?

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.970
So the first letter of 'Pride', then?

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:20.500
But, he said that those monsters'
names don't match their personalities.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:24.300
Which means that it has to be
either Greed, Lie or Envy.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:26.700
Ah, I don't know! Enough of this!

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:28.200
The next one! Next!

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.900
"My second and fourth begin
with the error in the twin."

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:35.800
Skip that, next!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:39.700
"My third begins a sparkle bright. The end is..."

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.400
Something shiny?

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:42.700
A star, maybe?

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.700
'S'?

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.000
Star?

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:46.400
Could this be it?

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.300
Diamond and Star!

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.900
Indeed, they do both shine.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:55.000
There's an empty space right here.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.350
The symbol hidden here must be the answer!

00:18:58.350 --> 00:18:59.400
Which one is it?

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:02.690
I get it!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:02.690
Huh?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:08.000
If we split this into blocks of four, the next
block always has one extra diamond in it.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:13.000
In other words, the symbol missing
from this blank space is a diamond!

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.400
I see!

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:18.350
So the third letter is the 'D' from 'Diamond'!

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:20.040
Alright, next!

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.700
"My second and fourth begin
with the error in the twin."

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:31.300
Lief, Barda, move the sofa!

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:37.300
There are two similar pictures on this carpet!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:40.000
So we just have to find the difference?

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.700
I found it!

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:44.600
The old man on the right
has a mole on his face!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.600
A bug...?!

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:50.000
No, the difference is in the buttons!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.000
The one on the left has one more button.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.900
So the answer is from 'Button', 'B'!

00:19:56.900 --> 00:20:00.400
Next is the name of the proud pet, then.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:04.170
Alright, leave this one
to me. I have a good idea.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:23.700
Hey guys, which one of you
is the coolest and strongest?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.000
Is that really going to work?!

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:28.500
It's not working!

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:29.800
Run away, quick!

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:31.650
So noisy...

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.650
Let's calm ourselves and rethink this.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.740
Remember what the Guardian said:

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:45.800
<i>Greed is feared by both the skilled liar, as well as the one with immense pride,</i>

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:53.000
Therefore, Greed is neither
the lying nor the proud one.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:58.800
The names and personalities don't match,
so Greed isn't the greedy one either.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:02.700
That's right! Which means that
Greed is the envious one!

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.300
So the Guardian really did give
us the right clues in the end...

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:11.850
And Pride once almost killed the greedy one.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:14.990
So, Pride is not the greedy one,

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:19.900
and because the names and personalities
don't match, it isn't the proud one either.

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:22.100
And it's not envious either!

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:25.000
Yes, because Greed is the envious one!

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:29.000
This means that Pride is the lying one, then!

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:33.000
Also, he said that Envy
doesn't have great pride.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:40.510
Envy is not envious, nor is he a liar,
since Pride is the lying one.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.400
Which means, Envy is the greedy one!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:48.500
With this, the name of the
proud one has been revealed!

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:49.800
"Lie"!

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:53.480
So it's the first letter of "Lie".

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:57.100
So according to that, the
Guardian's name is 'Lbdbu'.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.200
Well that can't be it.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:21:59.240
No, wait!

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.300
There is still one more clue in the mirror.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:07.200
"The end is the beginning, the last has two."?

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:08.800
What does it mean?

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:13.700
Maybe it's not the first letter,
but rather the last one?

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:20.600
So, the 'e' of 'Lie', the 'n' of 'Button',
the 'd' of 'Diamond'...

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:21.720
Endon!

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:23.600
It couldn't be!

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:24.510
No way!

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:27.500
The Guardian is... King Endon?!

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:53.180
I would be lying to you

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:58.980
if I said I wasn't lonely

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:05.480
I know I'm not being honest

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:11.280
but I just can't put it into words

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:18.330
It's for the sake of our dreams

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:21.830
At this point

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:27.500
to sing "I love you" to a faraway you

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:33.840
my voice would simply fade into the wind

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:40.140
In a way, that's worse than saying "goodbye"

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:47.230
But someday our dreams will bloom

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:55.620
Dreams X Dreams

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:08.200
<i>The Seven Gems: the Topaz.</i>

00:24:09.200 --> 00:24:12.700
<i>The first gem to be retrieved, it is the gem of Del.</i>

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:19.670
<i>It reveals the truth, opens the door to the spirit realm,
strengthens the soul, and cleanses the heart.</i>

00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:24.200
The monsters attack us
after we solve the puzzle.

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:27.500
On top of that, the Sorcerer
Orcus appears once again.

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:29.810
Who will win the gem?

00:24:30.730 --> 00:24:34.610
The Final Gem: The Diamond

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:33.800
Next time, 'The Final Gem: The Diamond'.

00:24:49.630 --> 00:24:54.630
See you next time
